<http://data.silknow.org/object/05d2e679-aa87-37aa-aed0-43d04f904349>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Cover, plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in straight stitches and back stitch, padded and quilted, backed with plain weave cotton.\nWhite ground.  The inner and outer borders contain a blue leafy meander with a red trefoil flower.  The main border has inward pointing stem with blue trefoil at its base and three red pointed flowers. This border has a quilted ground with a scale pattern. The quilting is worked with white silk.\nIn the centre is a lobed medallion formed by a blue band with red dots; there is a red and blue rosette in the centre.  A blue 8-pointed star encircles this and links 4 large red blossoms in profile at the diagonals and 4 round red blossoms at the cardinal points.  A pair of blue serrated leaves and a red trefoil emerges from the top of every blossom. On the outer edge of the lobed medallion there is a small red tree at every angle. A quarter of this design, minus tree, is in each corner.  The ground if filled with small sprigs with one star-like red flower and buds leaning to the left; these sprigs point towards the central horizontal axis.  The ground is quilted with the scale pattern.\nBacking: coarse white cotton through which the quilting has been worked. \nThere are five green silk twill loops on the back of the upper edge, for display purposes."@en , "quilted and embroidered, 1600-1799, Persian"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/97332a89-3717-3176-84b6-6b04d5c0702a> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/249e6e0d-6cc5-377e-b5d6-178f520fd6cd> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "quilted and embroidered, 1600-1799, Persian"@en , "Cover, plain weave cotton embroidered with silk in straight stitches and back stitch, padded and quilted, backed with plain weave cotton.\nWhite ground.  The inner and outer borders contain a blue leafy meander with a red trefoil flower.  The main border has inward pointing stem with blue trefoil at its base and three red pointed flowers. This border has a quilted ground with a scale pattern. The quilting is worked with white silk.\nIn the centre is a lobed medallion formed by a blue band with red dots; there is a red and blue rosette in the centre.  A blue 8-pointed star encircles this and links 4 large red blossoms in profile at the diagonals and 4 round red blossoms at the cardinal points.  A pair of blue serrated leaves and a red trefoil emerges from the top of every blossom. On the outer edge of the lobed medallion there is a small red tree at every angle. A quarter of this design, minus tree, is in each corner.  The ground if filled with small sprigs with one star-like red flower and buds leaning to the left; these sprigs point towards the central horizontal axis.  The ground is quilted with the scale pattern.\nBacking: coarse white cotton through which the quilting has been worked. \nThere are five green silk twill loops on the back of the upper edge, for display purposes."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/05d2e679-aa87-37aa-aed0-43d04f904349/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/05d2e679-aa87-37aa-aed0-43d04f904349/dimension/1> ;
